            <profile id="e7cb-d117-2bb7-7cee" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">To represent Balkan and Anatolian tribesmen, 0-3 units of Mountain Tribesmen or Barbarian Warriors may be chosen (see the rulebook, page 130). Mountain Tribesmen stats used; Barbarian Warriors not built. Trapezuntine, Morean and Epirote armies (may be Permanent Mercenaries). (Armies of Chivalry p.55)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="3cc4-d953-8f1e-07c2" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">6+ with Buckler +1 in hand-to-hand only</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
